1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:28,140
They're so beautiful when they're blooming, don't you think?

2
00:00:28,140 --> 00:00:28,860
Huh?

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,320
I think we can be together here, okay?

4
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:39,580
It's pretty private, so no one should see us.

5
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:43,220
I don't really care about that.

6
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:45,380
It's not like we're doing anything wrong, you know?

7
00:00:45,740 --> 00:00:46,940
Yeah, but...

8
00:00:46,940 --> 00:00:49,200
But what I do care about is being with you.

9
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:51,040
That's all I want.

10
00:00:56,940 --> 00:00:57,460
Sumika.

11
00:00:57,460 --> 00:01:00,100
I will never back down on my love.

12
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:01,880
Oh, Kureha.

13
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:02,920
I...

14
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:04,000
I won't either.

15
00:01:07,940 --> 00:01:08,500
Kureha!

16
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:11,120
A bear!

17
00:01:11,580 --> 00:01:12,480
There's a bear!

18
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:33,380
No way!

19
00:01:33,380 --> 00:01:36,060
A bear got over the Wall of Severance?

20
00:01:36,060 --> 00:01:37,720
What do we do?

21
00:01:38,860 --> 00:01:40,200
Don't worry, Sumika.

22
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:41,460
I'm here.

23
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:44,020
I won't let anything happen to you.

24
00:01:46,260 --> 00:01:49,240
From the beginning, we hated you.

25
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:53,280
But also, we loved you from the beginning as well.

26
00:01:54,180 --> 00:01:56,980
All we wanted was to become true friends with you.

27
00:01:56,980 --> 00:01:59,460
So we had to cross the Wall.

28
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:03,860
Kyuikuma!

29
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:07,340
Kyuikuma!

30
00:02:09,340 --> 00:02:10,220
Kyuikuma!

31
00:02:10,220 --> 00:02:10,840
Kyuikuma!

32
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:13,200
Kyuikuma!

33
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:13,740
Thank you.

34
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:14,940
Thank you.

35
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,080
Thank you.

36
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:16,580
Thank you.

37
00:02:16,620 --> 00:02:16,680
Thank you.

38
00:02:16,820 --> 00:02:17,700
Anyways, we'll see you.

39
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:18,920
Bye!

40
00:03:46,016 --> 00:03:48,016
Growl growl!

41
00:03:48,016 --> 00:03:51,016
Once upon a time, at the far reaches of space,

42
00:03:51,016 --> 00:03:54,016
the minor planet Kumaria exploded.

43
00:03:54,016 --> 00:03:56,016
The fragments of Kumaria that remained

44
00:03:56,016 --> 00:04:00,016
became a meteor swarm that rained down upon the Earth.

45
00:04:00,016 --> 00:04:05,016
That swarm made the world's bears rise up together as one.

46
00:04:05,016 --> 00:04:08,016
Then, they all started attacking humans.

47
00:04:08,016 --> 00:04:11,016
Like, who could have seen that coming, right?

48
00:04:11,016 --> 00:04:15,016
The humans then decided to build the Wall of Severance

49
00:04:15,016 --> 00:04:18,016
in an attempt to drive all the bears, like us,

50
00:04:18,016 --> 00:04:20,016
away from their world.

51
00:04:20,016 --> 00:04:21,016
But guess what?

52
00:04:21,016 --> 00:04:24,016
Silly old man-made rules don't work on bears!

53
00:04:24,016 --> 00:04:27,016
Do the math, humans! Growl!

54
00:04:27,016 --> 00:04:31,016
We are bears! We can't help that!

55
00:04:31,016 --> 00:04:33,016
Bears eat people!

56
00:04:33,016 --> 00:04:35,016
That's kind of like our thing!

57
00:04:35,016 --> 00:04:37,016
And so...

58
00:04:37,016 --> 00:04:40,016
Everyone, starting today you'll have some new friends.

59
00:04:40,016 --> 00:04:45,016
This is Ginko Yurishiro and Lulu Yurigasaki.

60
00:04:45,016 --> 00:04:47,016
Let's give them a warm welcome.

61
00:04:47,016 --> 00:04:48,016
Growl!

62
00:04:48,016 --> 00:04:50,016
We supposedly transferred here,

63
00:04:50,016 --> 00:04:51,016
but they don't know what we are

64
00:04:51,016 --> 00:04:53,016
because we're disguised as humans.

65
00:04:53,016 --> 00:04:54,016
He-he!

66
00:04:54,016 --> 00:04:58,016
Looks like nobody can tell we're bears so far!

67
00:04:58,016 --> 00:04:59,016
He-he!

68
00:04:59,016 --> 00:05:01,016
So many girls for Lulu to pick from!

69
00:05:01,016 --> 00:05:03,016
Sniff, sniff!

70
00:05:03,016 --> 00:05:04,016
It's heaven!

71
00:05:04,016 --> 00:05:07,016
The whole room smells delicious, Growl!

72
00:05:07,016 --> 00:05:10,016
This is perfect!

73
00:05:10,016 --> 00:05:13,016
Lulu is going to work hard so she can eat lots of girls!

74
00:05:13,016 --> 00:05:15,016
You too, right, Ginko?

75
00:05:15,016 --> 00:05:17,016
Oh, have you met Ginko Yurishiro yet?

76
00:05:17,016 --> 00:05:19,016
She's a bear too, of course.

77
00:05:19,016 --> 00:05:22,016
She's Lulu's darling and Lulu loves her

78
00:05:22,016 --> 00:05:24,016
and loves her to bits and bits and bits!

79
00:05:24,016 --> 00:05:29,016
Now then, girls, I'm sure most of you have heard the news already.

80
00:05:29,016 --> 00:05:32,016
But unfortunately, a couple of bears were sighted this morning

81
00:05:32,016 --> 00:05:35,016
on the roads very close to this school.

82
00:05:35,016 --> 00:05:37,016
I realize this is a shock.

83
00:05:37,016 --> 00:05:40,016
We considered it unthinkable for bears to cross the Wall of Severance

84
00:05:40,016 --> 00:05:42,016
and enter the human world.

85
00:05:42,016 --> 00:05:44,016
The warning has since been lifted,

86
00:05:44,016 --> 00:05:46,016
but you still need to be very careful.

87
00:05:46,016 --> 00:05:49,016
Even inside the school, make sure you're never alone.

88
00:05:49,016 --> 00:05:53,016
You should always have a friend with you.

89
00:05:53,016 --> 00:05:55,016
There she is!

90
00:05:58,016 --> 00:06:00,016
I finally found her.

91
00:06:00,016 --> 00:06:03,016
Yeah, I like how that girl smells.

92
00:06:03,016 --> 00:06:05,016
I bet she's delicious.

93
00:06:05,016 --> 00:06:07,016
Slurp!

94
00:06:07,016 --> 00:06:08,016
That Patty?

95
00:06:08,016 --> 00:06:09,016
They say something!

96
00:06:09,016 --> 00:06:10,016
Before you are out and come over,

97
00:06:10,016 --> 00:06:12,016
I have to ask her any questions.

98
00:06:12,016 --> 00:06:13,016
Someone likes me,

99
00:06:13,016 --> 00:06:14,016
I am sorry,

100
00:06:14,016 --> 00:06:15,396
I am sorry,

101
00:06:15,396 --> 00:06:16,716
we're going out of the taboon!

102
00:06:17,016 --> 00:06:20,016
Uhh, uhh.

103
00:06:20,016 --> 00:06:21,016
Sumika?

104
00:06:23,016 --> 00:06:28,016
OK, sorry, let's go.

105
00:06:28,016 --> 00:06:29,016
tom Exactly...

106
00:06:29,016 --> 00:06:30,016
There it be,

107
00:06:30,016 --> 00:06:31,016
eh,

108
00:06:32,016 --> 00:06:34,016
N livestream...

109
00:06:34,016 --> 00:06:41,636
Hey, Kureha. What do you like in your lunchbox?

110
00:06:42,316 --> 00:06:44,056
My lunchbox? Why?

111
00:06:44,056 --> 00:06:50,236
Well, I like chikawa fried and sui tempura. I was just wondering what you preferred.

112
00:06:51,036 --> 00:06:55,396
Let's see. I guess spaghetti and shiokara.

113
00:06:55,596 --> 00:06:57,316
Shiokara? Seriously?

114
00:06:58,196 --> 00:06:59,116
Is that weird?

115
00:06:59,116 --> 00:07:07,936
What? It's just, you like what old men eat.

116
00:07:08,776 --> 00:07:10,736
Old men? Yeah.

117
00:07:11,196 --> 00:07:17,616
That's not very nice. I mean, yeah, maybe it smells a little when I open my lunchbox, but so what?

118
00:07:18,076 --> 00:07:19,136
I love it.

119
00:07:19,656 --> 00:07:20,296
What?

120
00:07:20,976 --> 00:07:24,916
I don't care if you've got the palate of an old man. I love you anyway.

121
00:07:24,916 --> 00:07:29,036
I love you so much. And I always will.

122
00:07:29,116 --> 00:07:44,496
Sumika?

123
00:07:52,776 --> 00:07:53,856
Sumika!

124
00:07:53,856 --> 00:08:01,056
Kureha? Hey! Is something wrong?

125
00:08:01,476 --> 00:08:02,676
No. I just...

126
00:08:03,356 --> 00:08:07,716
Oh no! Did you not get to eat lunch?

127
00:08:09,116 --> 00:08:09,756
No.

128
00:08:09,756 --> 00:08:12,296
Here.

129
00:08:14,856 --> 00:08:17,576
Let's eat together. We can each take a half.

130
00:08:20,656 --> 00:08:23,096
There's chikawa in this roll, isn't there?

131
00:08:23,416 --> 00:08:25,456
Yeah, but it's not fried and tempura.

132
00:08:27,956 --> 00:08:29,056
What's so funny?

133
00:08:29,456 --> 00:08:29,896
Nothing.

134
00:08:29,896 --> 00:08:35,696
You know, I think we should eat here every day from now on.

135
00:08:35,916 --> 00:08:37,616
You mean it? Really?

136
00:08:38,716 --> 00:08:41,036
Yeah. I want to eat with you.

137
00:08:41,036 --> 00:08:46,456
I think food tastes better when we're together anyway. Do you think that too?

138
00:08:46,896 --> 00:08:47,416
I do.

139
00:08:47,416 --> 00:08:54,116
Growl, growl, growl, growl, growl.

140
00:08:54,116 --> 00:08:54,196
Growl, growl, growl.

141
00:08:54,716 --> 00:08:57,356
Lulu is practically starving right now.

142
00:08:57,456 --> 00:09:00,676
Oh, she smells so yummy. I want to eat that girl.

143
00:09:00,836 --> 00:09:01,436
Growl, growl.

144
00:09:01,976 --> 00:09:03,716
You are such a glutton, Ginkgo.

145
00:09:03,956 --> 00:09:06,576
But that's okay because Lulu will always love you.

146
00:09:06,756 --> 00:09:09,556
You can sink your teeth in Lulu anywhere you'd like.

147
00:09:09,836 --> 00:09:11,576
Come on, you can even do it now.

148
00:09:11,916 --> 00:09:13,916
Oh, Lulu can't believe she's saying this to you.

149
00:09:13,916 --> 00:09:17,496
Lulu feels so vulnerable when she's around you, Ginkgo.

150
00:09:43,916 --> 00:09:47,436
The storm chased us down.

151
00:09:48,396 --> 00:09:49,956
This is only the beginning.

152
00:09:50,676 --> 00:09:53,116
A warning that it'll start with what's most precious.

153
00:09:53,956 --> 00:09:57,016
The invisible storm will destroy whatever is in its path

154
00:09:57,016 --> 00:09:59,396
until we're worn away into nothing.

155
00:10:01,396 --> 00:10:04,656
Kureha, I'll never back down on my love either.

156
00:10:05,116 --> 00:10:05,676
What?

157
00:10:05,676 --> 00:10:09,236
You said it earlier, that you wouldn't give up on me.

158
00:10:09,756 --> 00:10:11,416
Well, I won't give up on you either.

159
00:10:11,836 --> 00:10:13,216
I won't give up on love.

160
00:10:13,796 --> 00:10:14,616
Our love.

161
00:10:15,336 --> 00:10:16,276
Growl, growl, growl.

162
00:10:16,496 --> 00:10:19,136
Lulu's so hungry she doesn't think she can take much more.

163
00:10:21,336 --> 00:10:22,236
Growl, growl.

164
00:10:22,296 --> 00:10:24,316
I cannot get over that delicious smell.

165
00:10:24,556 --> 00:10:25,336
Growl, growl.

166
00:10:27,676 --> 00:10:33,596
I still feel the same way.

167
00:10:33,596 --> 00:10:34,936
I won't back down.

168
00:10:35,496 --> 00:10:37,436
I promise I'll protect you, Sumika.

169
00:10:37,616 --> 00:10:39,116
I believe you.

170
00:10:44,256 --> 00:10:45,396
I knew it.

171
00:10:46,256 --> 00:10:49,556
I had a feeling you'd been caught up in the invisible storm too.

172
00:10:50,016 --> 00:10:51,576
You have, haven't you, Kureha?

173
00:10:51,996 --> 00:10:52,596
Mitsuko.

174
00:10:54,796 --> 00:10:56,716
It's cruel to cut down flowers,

175
00:10:57,216 --> 00:10:58,916
especially when they're in full bloom.

176
00:11:00,136 --> 00:11:01,816
It's the invisible storm.

177
00:11:01,816 --> 00:11:04,596
It destroys beautiful, kind things first.

178
00:11:04,956 --> 00:11:08,256
Yes, but this time what it's done has made up my mind.

179
00:11:08,736 --> 00:11:11,456
I can't just sit here and keep letting these things happen.

180
00:11:13,356 --> 00:11:16,696
Kureha, Sumika, let's stop the storm.

181
00:11:16,796 --> 00:11:18,116
We can take a stand together.

182
00:11:18,956 --> 00:11:20,576
I know I'm the class representative,

183
00:11:20,796 --> 00:11:24,156
but I'm ashamed of myself for not having taken a stand against it already.

184
00:11:24,936 --> 00:11:26,496
Sumika, I'm so sorry.

185
00:11:27,196 --> 00:11:29,076
Do you think you can ever forgive me?

186
00:11:29,656 --> 00:11:30,296
For what?

187
00:11:30,296 --> 00:11:31,416
There's nothing to forgive.

188
00:11:32,016 --> 00:11:33,336
Thank you for saying that.

189
00:11:33,396 --> 00:11:35,696
And you know, I think we could be the best of friends.

190
00:11:36,156 --> 00:11:38,076
I bet we can stop the invisible storm.

191
00:11:38,276 --> 00:11:40,356
As long as we're working together, why couldn't we?

192
00:11:40,356 --> 00:11:44,016
But I think we should go home for the day now.

193
00:11:44,196 --> 00:11:45,416
There's still that bear warning.

194
00:11:46,076 --> 00:11:48,616
I say, early tomorrow morning, we come back here.

195
00:11:48,856 --> 00:11:50,596
Then the flower bed can get fixed.

196
00:11:50,996 --> 00:11:52,436
I don't mind helping you at all.

197
00:11:54,016 --> 00:11:56,576
Oh no, your hand!

198
00:11:56,816 --> 00:11:57,736
No, it's okay.

199
00:11:57,996 --> 00:11:59,376
This just means I'm one of you.

200
00:11:59,676 --> 00:12:00,736
And that we're friends.

201
00:12:00,736 --> 00:12:22,456
Who did that?

202
00:12:22,456 --> 00:12:30,476
Lulu's so happy she got to eat a lily.

203
00:12:30,856 --> 00:12:32,596
Lulu wants to eat that girl.

204
00:12:32,876 --> 00:12:34,676
Who do you mean by that girl?

205
00:12:35,056 --> 00:12:36,816
Lulu wants to eat that girl.

206
00:12:37,096 --> 00:12:38,856
Who do you mean by that girl?

207
00:12:39,156 --> 00:12:41,036
Let's go on trial now.

208
00:12:41,256 --> 00:12:42,156
Yeah, let's go!

209
00:12:42,276 --> 00:12:42,636
Yeah!

210
00:12:42,636 --> 00:12:57,476
Kareha, did you have fun with your friend again today?

211
00:12:57,776 --> 00:12:58,176
Yep!

212
00:12:58,516 --> 00:12:59,336
Guess what, Mom?

213
00:12:59,516 --> 00:13:01,436
We ate snacks together at lunch!

214
00:13:02,296 --> 00:13:02,856
Great!

215
00:13:03,316 --> 00:13:04,156
Were they yummy?

216
00:13:04,436 --> 00:13:05,056
Mm-hmm!

217
00:13:05,376 --> 00:13:07,876
Everything tastes better when I get to eat them with her.

218
00:13:09,176 --> 00:13:11,756
Aw, you really love her, don't you, sweetie?

219
00:13:11,756 --> 00:13:13,276
Yeah, I do!

220
00:13:14,716 --> 00:13:18,076
Yes, and that's why this time the one I love will be safe.

221
00:13:19,816 --> 00:13:22,076
I'll protect her with my own hands.

222
00:13:22,556 --> 00:13:23,996
I'll never forgive the bears.

223
00:13:24,456 --> 00:13:25,356
I'll ruin them.

224
00:13:25,896 --> 00:13:26,756
Every one...

225
00:13:26,756 --> 00:13:26,856
Oh!

226
00:13:26,856 --> 00:13:27,856
Oh!

227
00:13:27,856 --> 00:13:27,956
Oh!

228
00:13:41,756 --> 00:13:46,096
Unit 103, we're at the flower bed in the Arashigaoka High School Courtyard.

229
00:13:46,716 --> 00:13:49,536
Lots of bear friends here, and blood stains.

230
00:13:49,536 --> 00:13:51,216
Looks like there was a Vic.

231
00:13:51,756 --> 00:13:53,236
We found her a fax at the scene.

232
00:13:53,616 --> 00:13:54,556
She may be a student.

233
00:13:55,036 --> 00:13:56,516
We're still searching the area, though.

234
00:13:57,676 --> 00:13:59,596
Yes, we were supposed to meet here.

235
00:14:00,496 --> 00:14:01,276
We were...

236
00:14:01,276 --> 00:14:03,616
We were gonna come early and fix up the flower bed.

237
00:14:03,616 --> 00:14:09,356
Your call has been forwarded to an automatic voicemail system.

238
00:14:09,756 --> 00:14:12,576
The mobile customer you are trying to reach is currently...

239
00:14:12,576 --> 00:14:16,356
I heard they found a shoe on the ground.

240
00:14:16,596 --> 00:14:17,336
They did?

241
00:14:17,696 --> 00:14:19,036
You know what that means.

242
00:14:19,396 --> 00:14:22,436
Apparently, she came in early to try and fix up that flower bed.

243
00:14:23,116 --> 00:14:23,996
Oh, gosh.

244
00:14:24,096 --> 00:14:25,256
It's so hard to believe.

245
00:14:25,496 --> 00:14:27,576
It's really her own fault for going alone.

246
00:14:27,876 --> 00:14:30,116
To survive, we need to make sure we have friends.

247
00:14:30,696 --> 00:14:31,676
Yeah, you're right.

248
00:14:31,956 --> 00:14:33,056
There's no other way.

249
00:14:33,576 --> 00:14:33,976
Uh-huh.

250
00:14:34,356 --> 00:14:36,076
The next invisible storm's coming.

251
00:14:36,076 --> 00:14:51,336
She's to blame since she wasn't being invisible.

252
00:14:51,756 --> 00:14:54,116
To the bears, we're just weak prey.

253
00:14:54,656 --> 00:14:56,176
We have to stay with the herd.

254
00:14:56,676 --> 00:14:57,596
No matter what.

255
00:14:57,916 --> 00:14:58,396
Exactly.

256
00:14:58,916 --> 00:15:00,936
The mood of the herd is what's most important.

257
00:15:04,016 --> 00:15:05,216
It's not true.

258
00:15:06,076 --> 00:15:07,076
It can't be!

259
00:15:11,796 --> 00:15:13,056
It's not true.

260
00:15:13,416 --> 00:15:15,416
I refuse to believe Sumika was eaten.

261
00:15:30,236 --> 00:15:30,836
Hello?

262
00:15:32,016 --> 00:15:32,616
Sumika?

263
00:15:32,616 --> 00:15:36,476
Is your love the real thing?

264
00:15:38,056 --> 00:15:40,456
This is a challenge from the Wall of Severance.

265
00:15:40,956 --> 00:15:41,956
Kareha Tsubaki.

266
00:15:42,456 --> 00:15:43,856
If your love is true,

267
00:15:44,956 --> 00:15:46,956
go to the roof immediately.

268
00:15:48,036 --> 00:15:49,836
The bears are waiting for you.

269
00:15:51,336 --> 00:15:52,196
What do you mean?

270
00:15:52,336 --> 00:15:53,156
Is Sumika okay?

271
00:15:53,156 --> 00:15:58,336
Give yourself over to the bears and your love will be approved.

272
